WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.343
[...]

00:00:04.343 --> 00:00:07.241
SPEAKER: In many countries,
it is against the law

00:00:07.241 --> 00:00:13.309
to hire a woman to be a surrogate
mother, to carry a pregnancy for pay.

00:00:13.309 --> 00:00:16.426
Some US states permit the practice.

00:00:16.426 --> 00:00:23.166
But the total cost is around $100,000,
more than many couples can afford.

00:00:23.166 --> 00:00:26.966
Seeking a more economical
alternative, many couples

00:00:26.971 --> 00:00:30.061
from Western countries
seeking surrogates now

00:00:30.066 --> 00:00:33.869
go to India, where
paid pregnancy is legal

00:00:33.869 --> 00:00:37.462
and a source of employment
for rural women.

00:00:37.462 --> 00:00:41.372
Indian women receive
around $6,000 to $8,000

00:00:41.372 --> 00:00:47.306
for caring a pregnancy, about
one-third of what surrogates in the US

00:00:47.306 --> 00:00:51.142
are paid but more than the Indian
surrogate mothers would otherwise

00:00:51.142 --> 00:00:54.232
earn in a lifetime.

00:00:54.236 --> 00:00:57.666
Suppose it were up to you,
as an Indian legislator,

00:00:57.669 --> 00:01:02.886
to decide whether to permit or
to prohibit commercial surrogacy.

00:01:02.886 --> 00:01:06.896
How would you vote?

